IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, piece cp5 -- MONTH HELPERS (infrastructure).
--
-- No provision of the Act licenses these rules: they carry no @ref. Part II counts in months and
-- picks "the latest of" months that apply only on some conditions (section 67), "the earliest of"
-- the events that end a benefit (sections 70, 70.02) and shifts months forward and back. A month
-- is the DATE of its first day (cpp-core-calendar.l4). `minimum` and `maximum` of the stable prelude
-- do not take DATEs (probed on 1.6.98), so the folds are written here. The names carry the piece
-- code so that no other piece can define the same name; NOTES.md, "Needs from the core", proposes
-- promoting them.

§ `Month helpers`

-- The later of two months, either of which may be absent. NOTHING means "that month does not apply".
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the later of two months that may not apply` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF x AT LEAST y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y

-- The earlier of two months, either of which may be absent.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the earlier of two months that may not apply` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y THEN IF x AT MOST y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y

-- The latest of the months that apply. NOTHING when none applies.
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the latest of the months that apply` months MEANS
    CONSIDER months
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `cp5 helper -- the later of two months that may not apply` m (`cp5 helper -- the latest of the months that apply` rest)

-- The earliest of the months that apply. NOTHING when none applies.
GIVEN months IS A LIST OF MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the earliest of the months that apply` months MEANS
    CONSIDER months
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `cp5 helper -- the earlier of two months that may not apply` m (`cp5 helper -- the earliest of the months that apply` rest)

-- The first day of the month that is a number of months after the month of a date (negative: before).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`cp5 helper -- the month a number of months from the month of a date` d n MEANS
    `add months` (`the month of a date` d) n

-- The month of an optional date, as an optional month.
GIVEN d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`the month of a date` x)

-- The month following the month of an optional date, as an optional month.
GIVEN d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the month following the month of a date that may be absent` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`the month following the month of a date` x)

-- A month kept only if it falls before a day; otherwise the rule that produced it does not apply.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE
      limit IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the month if it falls before a day` m limit MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x BELOW limit THEN JUST x ELSE NOTHING

-- A month kept only if it falls on or after a day.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE DATE
      limit IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the month if it falls on or after a day` m limit MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x AT LEAST limit THEN JUST x ELSE NOTHING

-- Whether a person is treated, for a provision that is not one of the ten excepted from section 2(2),
-- as having reached an age on a day. A wrapper over the core's rule, which needs the provision named.
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
      `on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`cp5 helper -- the person has reached an age on a day under section 2(2)` `date of birth` age `on` MEANS
    `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` age `on`

-- The month in which a person is treated, for a provision that is not one of the ten excepted from
-- section 2(2), as having reached an age (the month after the month of the birthday).
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`cp5 helper -- the month in which the person reaches an age under section 2(2)` `date of birth` age MEANS
    `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` age)

-- The day on which a person is treated, for a provision that is not one of the ten excepted from section 2(2),
-- as having reached an age (the first day of the month after the month of the birthday).
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`cp5 helper -- the day the person is treated as reaching an age under section 2(2)` `date of birth` age MEANS
    `s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` age

-- The first of several readings that gives a month, in the order they are listed.
GIVEN readings IS A LIST OF MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`cp5 helper -- the first reading that gives a month` readings MEANS
    CONSIDER readings
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER m
        WHEN JUST x THEN JUST x
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `cp5 helper -- the first reading that gives a month` rest

-- The later of two days.
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cp5 helper -- the later of two days` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b
